# Noebbly-attack.lic
# Bigshot custom attack routine for Noebbly (Paladin, falchion and greatshield). Drop it
# into a bigshot hunting-commands list as a single command, replacing
# "1603 (m3), shield bash (s10), kill (x3)":
#
#   script Noebbly-attack
#
# bigshot pauses itself, runs this once against the target it already has locked, then
# resumes to loot / wander / retarget -- so this does exactly ONE attack decision per
# call and returns; bigshot re-invokes it every pass while the target is still up. Same
# shape as Fizzlestiks-attack.lic.
#
# Rhythm (what that profile line did): bigshot expands it to Templar's Verdict (1603),
# a shield bash and three attacks, run top to bottom per target. This keeps that rhythm
# across calls in $noebbly_attack_rhythm ([target id, step 0-4]): a new target opens
# with the Verdict, then the bash, then three plain attacks, then the Verdict again.
#
#   step 0  Templar's Verdict, only if known and checkmana covers its real cost right
#           now (Spell#mana_cost, 3 if Lich has no number) -- the old (m3) gate.
#   step 1  shield bash, only if Lich's own Shield.available? says so (known, enough
#           stamina, off cooldown, not overexerted) -- the old (s10) gate, no stamina
#           number hardcoded here.
#   steps 2-4 / any slot whose move isn't available: a plain attack, the way a failed
#           (m3)/(s10) gate skipped that command.
#
# Written 11/19 from the 11/03 profile line and log (prepare 1603 / cast / shield bash
# #id); NOT run live yet.
#
# Disarm: nothing in the RIGHT hand (the shield is in the left) means the weapon is
# gone. Tries READY WEAPON once; if that fails too, asks bigshot to rest instead of
# punching -- Brayis died doing that.

# --- helpers -----------------------------------------------------------------

VERDICT = 1603 unless defined?(VERDICT)
VERDICT_FALLBACK_MANA = 3 unless defined?(VERDICT_FALLBACK_MANA)
CYCLE = 5 unless defined?(CYCLE)   # verdict, bash, three attacks

CAST_WAIT = /^\s*\.\.\.wait|^Wait \d+ sec/i unless defined?(CAST_WAIT)
CAST_DONE = /Cast Roundtime \d+ Sec|Roundtime: \d+ sec|can't think clearly enough to prepare|^\s*\.\.\.wait|^Wait \d+ sec/i unless defined?(CAST_DONE)
CANT_CAST_WOUNDED = /can't think clearly enough to prepare a spell/i unless defined?(CANT_CAST_WOUNDED)

# Monster-agnostic death check: bigshot itself never text-matches kill messages --
# it reads GameObj status, which Lich keeps current. "dead" while the corpse lingers,
# "gone" once it decays or is looted.
def target_dead?(foe)
  return true if foe.nil?
  return true if foe.status.to_s =~ /dead|gone/
  !GameObj.targets.any? { |t| t.id.to_i == foe.id.to_i && t.status.to_s !~ /dead|gone/ }
end

def verdict_mana
  cost = (Spell[VERDICT].mana_cost.to_i rescue 0)
  cost.positive? ? cost : VERDICT_FALLBACK_MANA
end

# Sends cmd and collects every line through the cast roundtime.
def cast_collect(cmd, timeout = 6)
  lines = []
  clear
  put cmd
  deadline = Time.now.to_f + timeout
  loop do
    line = get?
    if line.nil?
      sleep 0.1
    else
      lines << line
      break if line =~ CAST_DONE
    end
    break if Time.now.to_f >= deadline
  end
  lines.join("\n")
end

# Plain attack with whatever is in hand. No-ops if the target is already dead.
def plain_attack(foe)
  return if target_dead?(foe)
  fput "attack"
  waitrt?
end

# Templar's Verdict at the locked target.
# @return [Boolean] true if a cast was actually sent
def try_verdict(foe)
  return false unless Spell[VERDICT].known?
  return false if checkmana < verdict_mana
  waitcastrt?
  waitrt?
  return false if target_dead?(foe)
  return false if checkmana < verdict_mana   # re-read right before the cast
  text = cast_collect("incant #{VERDICT}")
  if text =~ CAST_WAIT
    # Right after a swing Lich may not have registered its roundtime yet, so waitrt?
    # alone returns at once and the retry is refused too: sleep what the game said.
    secs = text[/wait (\d+) sec/i, 1].to_i
    sleep([secs, 5].min) if secs.positive?
    waitrt?
    waitcastrt?
    return false if target_dead?(foe) || checkmana < verdict_mana
    text = cast_collect("incant #{VERDICT}")
  end
  return false if text =~ CANT_CAST_WOUNDED
  true
end

# Shield bash if Lich says it's usable right now. Shield.use waits out roundtime
# first and returns the answering line, or nil if it never sent anything.
# @return [Boolean] true if a bash was actually sent
def try_bash(foe)
  return false unless Shield.available?("bash", target: foe)
  !Shield.use("bash", foe).nil?
end

def handle_disarmed
  echo "########## NO WEAPON IN RIGHT HAND -- not fighting bare-fisted ##########"
  echo "## asking bigshot to rest"
  $bigshot_should_rest = true
  $rest_reason = "Disarmed"
end

# --- main ----------------------------------------------------------------

foe = GameObj.targets.find { |t| t.id.to_i == XMLData.current_target_id.to_i } if XMLData.current_target_id
foe ||= GameObj.targets.find { |t| t.status.to_s !~ /dead|gone/ }

# nothing (live) to hit -- hand control straight back to bigshot, which loots
exit if target_dead?(foe)

fput "target ##{foe.id}" unless XMLData.current_target_id.to_i == foe.id.to_i

waitrt?
waitcastrt?

exit if target_dead?(foe)

if checkright.nil?
  fput "ready weapon"
  pause 0.5
  if checkright.nil?
    handle_disarmed
    exit
  end
end

fput "stance offensive" if stance != "offensive"

last_id, step = $noebbly_attack_rhythm
step = 0 unless last_id == foe.id   # new target: open with the Verdict
step = step.to_i % CYCLE

did = case step
      when 0 then try_verdict(foe)
      when 1 then try_bash(foe)
      else false
      end
plain_attack(foe) unless did
$noebbly_attack_rhythm = [foe.id, (step + 1) % CYCLE]
